  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed installation of an air source heat pump at would constitute permitted development under Schedule 2, Part 14, Class G of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015 (as amended), and planning permission is therefore not required.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The heat pump would comply with the MCS Planning Standards (MCS 020(a)) as required by paragraph G.1;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The proposal is for two heat pump(s) on a detached dwellinghouse&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;No wind turbine is installed or proposed within the curtilage&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The dwellinghouse is not a listed building, is not within the curtilage of one, and is not on a site designated as a scheduled monument&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The outdoor compressor units would not exceed 1.5 m³&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The unit would not be installed on a pitched roof&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The site is in the Wool Road Conservation Area. However, the the unit would not be on a wall or roof fronting a highway, nor nearer to the highway than the dwellinghouse,&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;It would not be installed on a wall fronting a highway above ground-floor level&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The development is subject to the conditions in paragraph G.3. The heat pump must not be used solely for cooling. It must, so far as practicable, be sited to minimise its effect on the external appearance of the building and on the amenity of the area. It must be removed as soon as reasonably practicable when no longer needed for or capable of microgeneration.&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
